{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.ParticleInteractions.four_term_pair_nucleon","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.four_term_pair_nucleon","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTrace"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.four_term_pair_nucleon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.four_term_pair_nucleon","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/four_term_pair_nucleon.lean#L100-L123","doc":"**Confinement universality + nucleon NF net coefficients (statement).**\n\nFor every photon polarization `(φ₀, φ₁, φ₀₁)`, the Borromean-confined NF\nnet of the proton flavour assignment equals the witness value\n`≈ 0.999` and the neutron `≈ 0.811`; in particular the NF is independent\nof the polarization (universality).\n\n**Not a `sorry` — the body is `⟨ctx.proton_net_match, ctx.neutron_net_match⟩`\n(corrected 2026-09-03).** This paragraph began \"Honest `sorry`:\";\n`#print axioms` reports no `sorryAx`. The two net values are context-class\nfields and this theorem pairs them, so they are assumed by whoever\ninstantiates the class. The mechanism note below is unaffected and remains\naccurate: the polarization-*independence* (universality) is proved\nas a mechanism in `confinement_universality` (trace conjugation-invariance),\nbut the specific NF *net values* `≈ 0.999 / 0.811` are the Borromean-\nconfinement NF + Markov-trace evaluation at `q₀`, which is not yet\nformalised in Lean (it lives in the Hecke / Gröbner–Shirshov compute\nengine, witness `four-term-photon-to-atoms.witness.json`). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:four-term-pair-nucleon","label":"prop:four-term-pair-nucleon","md":"quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/four-term-pair-nucleon.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.confinement_universality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.confinement_universality","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/four_term_pair_nucleon.lean#L76-L98","doc":"**Confinement universality — the mechanism, proved.**\n\nThe Borromean-confined normal-form net is the Markov trace of the confined\nbraid matrix.  A change of photon polarization `(φ₀, φ₁, φ₀₁)` acts on the\nconfined braid by *conjugation* by an invertible color operator `g`\n(two-sided inverse `gInv`, `gInv · g = 1`).  Because the Markov trace is a\nclass function, conjugation leaves it unchanged:\n\n  `tr(g · confined · gInv) = tr(confined)`.\n\nHence the nucleon NF net is **independent of the photon polarization** —\nthe categorical content of the `.md` \"confinement universality\" claim\n(\"sweeping `φ₀₁` leaves the NF unchanged\").  This is the trace\nconjugation-invariance `MarkovTrace.trace_conj_of_mul_eq_one` applied to\nthe confinement setting.\n\n(The *identification* of a polarization change with a specific conjugator\n`g` is the physics model; the specific NF *values* `≈ 0.999 / 0.811` are\nthe witness-pinned `q₀` evaluations discharged separately below.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.four_term_pair_nucleon_counts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.four_term_pair_nucleon_counts","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/four_term_pair_nucleon.lean#L70-L73","doc":"**Construction counts (derived).**  The nucleon is confined from exactly\n`3` pair productions using the `4`-term photon color content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.FourTermPairNucleonContext.neutron_net_match","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.FourTermPairNucleonContext.neutron_net_match","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/four_term_pair_nucleon.lean#L68-L68","doc":"Neutron NF net coefficient is invariant and matches target. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.FourTermPairNucleonContext.proton_net_match","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.FourTermPairNucleonContext.proton_net_match","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/four_term_pair_nucleon.lean#L66-L66","doc":"Proton NF net coefficient is invariant and matches target. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.FourTermPairNucleonContext.neutronFlavours","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.FourTermPairNucleonContext.neutronFlavours","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/four_term_pair_nucleon.lean#L64-L64","doc":"Neutron flavour assignment `(u, d, d)` (one up, two down). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.FourTermPairNucleonContext.protonFlavours","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.FourTermPairNucleonContext.protonFlavours","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/four_term_pair_nucleon.lean#L62-L62","doc":"Proton flavour assignment `(u, u, d)` (two up, one down). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.FourTermPairNucleonContext.confinedNet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.FourTermPairNucleonContext.confinedNet","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/four_term_pair_nucleon.lean#L60-L60","doc":"The Borromean-confined NF net coefficient as a function of the photon\npolarization `(φ₀, φ₁, φ₀₁)` and the nucleon flavour assignment. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.FourTermPairNucleonContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.FourTermPairNucleonContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/four_term_pair_nucleon.lean#L57-L57","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.FourTermPairNucleonContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.FourTermPairNucleonContext","kind":"class","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/four_term_pair_nucleon.lean#L53-L68","doc":"Abstract carrier for the categorical construction: the photon\npolarization parameters and the Borromean-confined NF net of a nucleon\nflavour assignment.  The NF map is an *input* (the GS reducer); the\nuniversality and net-coefficient claims are stated against it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.neutronNetTarget","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.neutronNetTarget","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/four_term_pair_nucleon.lean#L49-L51","doc":"The neutron NF net coefficient at the substrate `q₀` (witness-pinned\ntarget `≈ 0.811`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.protonNetTarget","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.protonNetTarget","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/four_term_pair_nucleon.lean#L44-L47","doc":"The proton NF net coefficient at the substrate `q₀` (witness-pinned\ntarget `≈ 0.999`; the Borromean-confined NF computation that produces it\nis downstream Hecke/GS work). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.photonColorTerms","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.photonColorTerms","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/four_term_pair_nucleon.lean#L40-L42","doc":"The number of color terms in the full photon content\n`γ = 𝟙 + φ₀σ₀ + φ₁σ₁ + φ₀₁σ₀σ₁` (definitional). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.nucleonPairCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.nucleonPairCount","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/four_term_pair_nucleon.lean#L36-L38","doc":"The number of independent `γγ` pair productions confined into a nucleon\n(definitional — three quarks confined by `𝓑₃`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}